# Only NON-secret, browser-exposed configuration belongs here. Vite inlines
# every VITE_-prefixed variable into the client bundle, so never put backend
# secrets, database URLs, or API keys behind this prefix.
#
# There is no API-base-URL variable here on purpose: the API client
# (src/lib/apiClient.ts) always calls a same-origin relative /api/v1/...
# path, proxied to the backend by Vite in dev (vite.config.ts) or by nginx
# in production (nginx.conf) — see both compose files.

# Must match the backend's ADMIN_ROUTE_PREFIX (server/.env) exactly — the
# admin API is mounted at /api/v1/<that value> instead of the predictable
# /api/v1/admin, as defense-in-depth against automated scanners. Baked into
# the built JS bundle like every other VITE_-prefixed var, so it is NOT a
# secret by itself — but this is a public demo with a published demo-admin
# account, so pick a non-default value anyway.
VITE_ADMIN_ROUTE_PREFIX=admin
